<title>SINGAPORE: RTRS-Singapore Airlines increases flights.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Singapore Airlines increases flights.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Airlines said on Thursday it would increase the number of its flights to several cities in Asia and Europe.</p>
<p>The airline said in a statement it would add one flight a week to the destinations.</p>
<p>That meant there would now be three flights a week to Athens and the Chinese city of Guangzhou, four to New Delhi and the north English city of Manchester, seven to Dhaka, 11 to the Indonesian city of Surabaya and 12 to Ho Chi Minh City.</p>
<p>The airline also said its three flights a week to Dharan would be replaced by three trips to Jeddah and one of its four weekly flights to Adelaide would be cut.</p>
</text>
